# Keeps secrets and state out of every image build context.
# Every `docker build` in this repo that uses backend/ as its context (the llm-proxy image:
# `docker build -t forge-llm-proxy:latest -f docker/llm-proxy/Dockerfile .`) sends the whole
# directory to the daemon, and backend/ holds the real LLM key in `.env`.
# The llm-proxy image copies only `constraints.txt` and `app/`; nothing below is needed by any image.
# tests/test_dockerignore.py pins this file.

# A .dockerignore pattern is anchored at the context root (unlike .gitignore, `*.db` does NOT match
# `tests/x.db`), so the patterns that must hold at any depth start with `**/`.

# Credentials and operator configuration
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env

# State: the platform DB (and SQLite's sidecar files), service-database dumps, every service's repo
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
local-git/
backups/

# Environments, caches, logs, build output
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
**/*.log
.git/
